WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.542
Module four, the last module. Live chat and customer care.

2
00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:08.736
What to do when customers reply, and how to keep the number safe.

3
00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:16.234
This is the heart of customer care. Every reply, question and complaint arrives in

4
00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:21.664
Live chat. How fast and how well you answer decides what customers think of Oribrix.

5
00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:23.970
First, the live chat inbox.

6
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.510
Then tags, history and contacts.

7
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.560
Then agents and their roles.

8
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.018
Then opt-out management, which keeps the number safe.

9
00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:34.452
Then welcome and away messages.

10
00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:37.846
And finally, chatbot flows and integrations.

11
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:43.305
Here's what happens when a customer writes to Oribrix.

12
00:00:43.755 --> 00:00:47.040
The message arrives in Live chat, from the menu on the left.

13
00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.133
Agents get a notification.

14
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.383
An agent picks up the conversation. A manager can also step in at any time.

15
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:59.805
The agent replies. Inside the twenty four hour window you can write freely, with no

16
00:00:59.805 --> 00:01:00.764
Template needed.

17
00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:05.800
The agent tags the chat, for example hot lead, complaint or order issue.

18
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.147
After twenty four hours, the chat moves to History, where you can still find it and

19
00:01:11.147 --> 00:01:12.032
Filter by tags.

20
00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:18.317
This is the most important rule in customer care on WhatsApp.

21
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:23.601
After a customer's last message, you have twenty four hours to reply with any text.

22
00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:28.631
Once that window closes, you can only restart the conversation with an approved

23
00:01:28.631 --> 00:01:33.916
Template. So answer customers the same day. A late reply costs more and feels worse

24
00:01:33.916 --> 00:01:34.934
To the customer.

25
00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.208
Good records make follow-up easy.

26
00:02:25.658 --> 00:02:30.941
Tags are your own labels. Create a small, fixed set, like hot lead, complaint,

27
00:02:30.941 --> 00:02:34.192
Refund, vendor enquiry, and use them every time.

28
00:02:34.642 --> 00:02:37.372
History keeps chats older than twenty four hours.

29
00:02:37.822 --> 00:02:42.708
Contacts holds everyone who messaged Oribrix or was messaged in a campaign.

30
00:02:43.158 --> 00:02:46.336
You can import contact lists, and export the database.

31
00:02:46.786 --> 00:02:50.968
Filter contacts by tags and attributes, and broadcast to that group.

32
00:02:51.418 --> 00:02:53.636
And manage blocked and opted-in numbers.

33
00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:59.062
You can add up to fifteen team members, each with a role.

34
00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:04.976
The owner sees and controls everything, including billing, settings and the API key.

35
00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:07.448
Keep this to one or two senior people.

36
00:03:07.898 --> 00:03:11.866
A manager runs the team: campaigns, reports and live chat.

37
00:03:12.316 --> 00:03:15.675
An agent has access only to live chat and campaigns.

38
00:03:15.675 --> 00:03:21.099
Most customer care staff should be agents. Give each person their own login, never a

39
00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:21.810
Shared one.

40
00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:29.165
If customers block or report the Oribrix number, Meta can lower its limits or

41
00:03:29.165 --> 00:03:32.776
Restrict it. Opt-out management is how you prevent that.

42
00:03:33.226 --> 00:03:38.026
When a customer replies with words like stop, unsubscribe or not interested,

43
00:03:38.476 --> 00:03:41.441
The platform marks them as opted out automatically.

44
00:03:41.891 --> 00:03:44.835
From the next campaign on, they won't receive messages.

45
00:03:45.285 --> 00:03:49.552
Fewer blocks and reports keep the number healthy and the daily limit growing.

46
00:03:50.002 --> 00:03:55.399
And never add opted-out people back by hand. Respecting a no is good customer care.

47
00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:02.600
Under Manage and the settings menu, set these once, and they work for you every day.

48
00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.402
A welcome message, sent automatically when someone writes for the first time.

49
00:04:07.852 --> 00:04:12.396
An away message for off hours, so customers know when to expect a reply.

50
00:04:12.846 --> 00:04:16.323
Working hours, so the platform knows when the team is on and off.

51
00:04:16.773 --> 00:04:21.787
Campaign safety. If a template's category changes midway, the campaign stops.

52
00:04:22.237 --> 00:04:23.858
Analytics by day and month.

53
00:04:24.308 --> 00:04:28.788
And billing and usage, plus notification settings for phone or laptop.

54
00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.212
A chatbot answers common questions automatically, day and night.

55
00:04:35.212 --> 00:04:38.347
You can build up to five flows with drag and drop.

56
00:04:38.797 --> 00:04:40.162
Open the flow builder.

57
00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:44.623
Drag in a start message, like welcome to Oribrix, how can we help?

58
00:04:45.073 --> 00:04:50.129
Add buttons or a list: track my order, prices, become a vendor, talk to support.

59
00:04:50.579 --> 00:04:55.424
Add actions, like sending media, asking for a location, or showing a product

60
00:04:55.424 --> 00:04:56.061
Catalogue.

61
00:04:56.511 --> 00:04:59.733
Connect a branch to a human agent, or to another flow.

62
00:05:00.183 --> 00:05:05.495
Click Active, and save. The flow is now live. Always keep a talk to support option,

63
00:05:05.495 --> 00:05:08.183
So customers never get stuck with the bot.

64
00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:14.706
Finally, the standards every Oribrix customer care agent should follow.

65
00:05:15.156 --> 00:05:18.526
Reply the same day, inside the twenty four hour window.

66
00:05:18.976 --> 00:05:22.496
Greet customers by name, and keep messages short and clear.

67
00:05:22.946 --> 00:05:26.168
Tag every chat, so anyone can pick up where you left off.

68
00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:31.759
Never share O T Ps, passwords or the API key, in chat or anywhere else.

69
00:05:32.209 --> 00:05:33.468
Respect opt-outs.

70
00:05:33.918 --> 00:05:37.822
And escalate refunds and complaints to the right person the same day.

71
00:05:40.233 --> 00:05:44.600
Last quick check. A customer wrote thirty hours ago, and nobody replied.

72
00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.572
How can you message them now? Think for a moment.

73
00:05:51.522 --> 00:05:56.361
The answer: only with an approved template, because the twenty four hour window has

74
00:05:56.361 --> 00:05:56.770
Closed.

75
00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.231
Let's recap the whole course.

76
00:06:01.681 --> 00:06:06.566
Module one. A fresh number, business documents, daily limits and the dashboard.

77
00:06:07.016 --> 00:06:10.920
Module two. Templates in three categories, approved by Meta.

78
00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:16.640
Module three. CSV broadcasts, analytics, and the API with a secret key.

79
00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:22.355
Module four. The twenty four hour window, tags, roles, opt-outs and the chatbot.

80
00:06:22.355 --> 00:06:27.159
Now try the practice quiz, then take the final quiz for your certificate.

81
00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:33.323
That's the end of module 4. You've completed all four modules.

82
00:06:33.323 --> 00:06:35.988
Now take the quiz, and get your certificate.
